---
id: PY-007
type: rule
family: python-reliability
title: 'Any annotation escapes the type system'
version: 1

severity: warning
confidence: medium
spectrum_position: 2

targets: [source]
file_extensions: [.py]
allowlist: ['**/test_*.py', '**/*_test.py', '**/tests/**', '**/conftest.py', '**/explain/**']

detection:
  type: regex
  pattern: ':\s*(\w+\.)*Any\b|->\s*(\w+\.)*Any\b|\[[^\]]*\bAny\b'

related: [PY-001]
enabled: true
opt_in: true
---

`Any` switches off type checking for the value it annotates and everything
derived from it, so the checker can no longer catch misuse downstream. Reach for
a real type, a `Protocol`, a `TypeVar`, or `object` (which keeps the checks)
before `Any`. This rule is opt-in because partially-typed code legitimately uses
`Any` at boundaries; enable it for fully-typed packages.
